  "body": "Closes #366\nClaim: mac/lot-366\n\n**Problem.** `ForumSessionCheckTests` failed at random on the simulator CI, never the same test twice: `loginSavedWhileACheckWritesBackWinsOverItsCookies` (run 41232795746) and `loginDuringARecheckWinsOverItsResult` (run 41323654034). Reruns passed.\n\n**Cause.** Five tests ran under `.timeLimit(.minutes(1))`. Swift Testing starts that clock before the test gets the main actor, and every app test shares the main actor. On the `xcode-27` runner, untimed tests that do milliseconds of work report 30–40 s in a normal run and up to 120 s in the failing runs (run 41232795746: `TopicReaderModelTests` and others passed at 119.9 s, while the timed test failed at exactly 60.000 s). So the limit measured the main-actor queue, not the test. When it fires, Xcode treats the test as hung and kills the runner process. That is why the second failure has no `Test case` line in the log, and only 155 of the 349 results were printed.\nReproduced locally: run next to a throwaway test that holds the main actor for 65 s, `recheckWhileTheLaunchCheckWaitsOnAnotherAccountSendsNothing` failed with \"Test exceeded execution time allowance of 1 minute\" at 60.000 s. Run in isolation, the suite passed 50 iterations under full CPU load (500/500): the model has no race.\n\n**Change.** `CheckGate.entered()` now also returns when the gated work calls `finish()` without reaching the gate. It returns whether the gate was reached, and the tests `#require` that. A guard that skips the gated call now fails at once. That hang was the only reason for the time limits, so the limits are removed. The two other `CheckGate` users (`AccountsModelTests`, `AccountsModelLoginTests`) had the same possible hang and now use the same pattern. No app code changes.\n\n**Tests.**\n- Same 65 s main-actor hog with the fix: all 10 `ForumSessionCheckTests` pass, at about 65.5 s each.\n- A gate that is never reached (gated call moved to 9, temporarily) fails in 0.026 s with \"the re-check never reached the gate\", where it used to hang until the limit.\n- `ForumSessionCheckTests` + `AccountsModelTests` + `AccountsModelLoginTests`: 100 iterations under CPU load (20 `yes` processes), 2100 passed, 0 failed.\n- Full app suite: 3 iterations, 1047 passed, 0 failed (iPhone 18 Pro, iOS 27.0 simulator clone).\n\nNote: the main actor is held for long stretches on the CI runner, which is visible in the durations of every suite. Any future wall-clock limit on an app test would be flaky in the same way.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFA3L8YfjJi4AdxgzW\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Improved reliability of account login, restore, and session-check concurrency tests. Tests now verify that expected checkpoints are reached and handle work completing before a checkpoint.\n  * Removed wall-clock time limits from several concurrency tests.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
