   "body": "Adversarial review (Sonnet), head 78f55a1f1902ee9d991307c8c82636ea5b2bc37b: **REQUEST CHANGES**\n1. (major) Root cause and repeat count not shown. **Answered, no change.** The evidence is in the PR body and on #366, outside the diff the reviewer had. Reproduction: a 65 s main-actor hold made a timed test fail at 60.000 s with \"exceeded execution time allowance\". CI durations: untimed tests passed at 119.9 s in the failing run. Isolation: 500/500 iterations under load before the fix. Repeat counts after the fix: 2100/2100 for the three suites over 100 iterations under load, and 1047/1047 for the full suite over 3 iterations. The gate-less `loginSavedWhile…` failure at 60.000 s, while untimed tests passed at 119.9 s in the same run, points to queueing, not a deadlock. Its only awaits are a scripted login and `Mutex` reads.\n2. (minor) Removing `.timeLimit` drops the protection against deadlocks. **Answered, kept as is.** A limit of any size is a wall clock on the shared main actor: CI already showed 120 s of queueing, so 5 min would only make the flake rarer. The hang it was written for (a skipped gate) now fails at once (shown in 0.026 s). A real deadlock still ends at the job timeout, with Xcode's hang report naming the test.\n3. (nit) `finish()` is a manual convention. **Fixed** in 04dc941a9f02efe2749ef0c934d4ad6cb7d8dce3: `CheckGate.run { … }` calls it, and all six gate tests use it. Rerun: 100 iterations under load, 2100 passed, 0 failed.\n",
